{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ccb18EkmD4iTaz4aLAiFu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for paper submission ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: exp-001\n5\t    claim: 1  # Item dominance at scale\n6\t    registry_id: exp001_llama  # also: exp001_gemma, exp001_mistral, exp001_qwen\n7\t    description: >\n8\t      Full-scale precision study: 4 models (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, Gemma-2-9B-IT, Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3)\n9\t      × 3 precisions (FP32, BF16, FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings\n10\t      × 200 MMLU items (stratified). All precisions use consistent vLLM engine (V0 enforce_eager)\n11\t      to eliminate the float32 engine confound found in MVP. Validates item dominance finding at\n12\t      scale and with multiple models.\n13\t    priority: P0\n14\t    gpu_budget_hours: 100\n15\t    hardware: westd-32570 (RTX PRO 6000 96GB)\n16\t    deps: []\n17\t    status: done\n18\t\n19\t  - id: exp-001b\n20\t    claim: 1  # Item dominance stability across item samples\n21\t    registry_id: exp001b_resampling\n22\t    description: >\n23\t      Item resampling stability test: 3 independent stratified samples of 200 MMLU items\n24\t      (seeds 0, 7, 99) × 1 model (Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) × 3 precisions × 3 prompts\n25\t      × 3 seeds × 2 orderings = 54 conditions per sample. Tests whether the 58% item\n26\t      dominance finding is stable across different item draws from MMLU, not an artifact\n27\t      of the specific 200-item sample. Critical for defending the headline claim.\n28\t    priority: P0\n29\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n30\t    hardware: westd-32570\n31\t    deps: [exp-001]\n32\t    status: done\n33\t\n34\t  - id: exp-002\n35\t    claim: 1  # Item dominance generalizes + cross-benchmark gradient (also supports claim 3: benchmark-conditional budget)\n36\t    registry_id: exp002_multi_benchmark\n37\t    description: >\n38\t      Multi-benchmark replication (D009 expanded): 8 models × 5 benchmarks × BF16 × 2 temps\n39\t      × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 4 orderings × 200 items each.\n40\t      Phase 1 (RUNNING): 4 original models × 4 benchmarks (MMLU/ARC/HellaSwag/GSM8K) on westd-32570.\n41\t      Phase 2: + MATH as 5th benchmark (all models).\n42\t      Phase 3: + Yi-1.5-9B, OLMo-2-7B on all 5 benchmarks (westd-15695).\n43\t      Phase 4: + InternLM2.5-7B, DeepSeek-7B on all 5 benchmarks.\n44\t      Validates cross-benchmark variance gradient, permutation test for monotonicity,\n45\t      and benchmark-conditional D-study budgets.\n46\t    priority: P0\n47\t    gpu_budget_hours: 300\n48\t    hardware: westd-32570 + westd-15695\n49\t    deps: [exp-001]\n50\t    status: running\n51\t\n52\t  - id: exp-003\n53\t    claim: 2  # Separability with hardware factor\n54\t    description: >\n55\t      Multi-hardware G-study: 4 models × 2+ GPU types × 2 precisions (BF16, FP16)\n56\t      × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items.\n57\t      Tests hardware × methodology interaction. Descoped from current priority —\n58\t      infrastructure claim narrowed to \"precision separability\" per D003/D007.\n59\t      Would strengthen paper if second GPU type becomes available.\n60\t    priority: P1\n61\t    gpu_budget_hours: 120\n62\t    hardware: TBD (needs different GPU type)\n63\t    deps: []\n64\t    status: descoped\n65\t\n66\t  - id: exp-004\n67\t    claim: 3  # D-study reproducibility budget\n68\t    description: >\n69\t      Comprehensive analysis of combined exp-001/001b/002/003 data. Includes:\n70\t      (a) Model-as-facet G-theory reanalysis — treat model as crossed random facet to properly\n71\t      attribute model×item interaction and reduce inflated item_id/residual (Dream critical);\n72\t      (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) on ALL variance components in ALL tables, especially\n73\t      direct infra×method interaction term (Dream critical);\n74\t      (c) D-study projections with CIs for optimal allocation across facets for G≥0.90/0.95/0.99,\n75\t      with benchmark-specific budgets and comparison to IRT-based subsampling (tinyBenchmarks);\n76\t      (d) REML vs Henderson Method I comparison as sensitivity analysis;\n77\t      (e) Logprob-based scoring as third response variable;\n78\t      (f) Ranking stability analysis — does precision×temperature interaction alter model rankings?\n79\t      (g) Higher-order interaction estimation to decompose the residual component;\n80\t      (h) G-theory vs IRT direct comparison — same MMLU data, D-study vs tinyBenchmarks IRT\n81\t      subsampling, compare recommended item counts and discuss why G-theory is more conservative\n82\t      (accounts for prompt/seed dimensions IRT ignores). First direct comparison in the literature;\n83\t      (i) Power analysis — verify statistical power to detect ≥X% interaction effects given\n84\t      5184×200 design scale, preempt \"underpowered\" reviewer concern;\n85\t      (j) Practitioner evaluation protocol guide (Discussion/Appendix);\n86\t      (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity — rerun G-study with temperature/ordering as fixed facets,\n87\t      compare variance decomposition (MD2 defense);\n88\t      (l) Binary data limitation analysis — correlate Bernoulli p(1-p) with observed item variance,\n89\t      parallel binary vs text_exact_match analysis (MD1 defense);\n90\t      (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife CI comparison — delete-1 jackknife as independence-safe alternative,\n91\t      compare CI widths (MD6 defense);\n92\t      (n) Cross-benchmark design asymmetry sensitivity — re-analyze MMLU with matched 2×2 design\n93\t      (bf16/fp16 × T=0.0/T=0.7), compare with full 3×3 (MD8 defense);\n94\t      (o) G-coefficient at full benchmark size — D-study projection to 14K MMLU items (MD5 defense);\n95\t      (p) Logprob-based scoring across all benchmarks — expand from MMLU-only to all 5 benchmarks,\n96\t      support \"Evaluation Metrics\" in title (MD9 defense);\n97\t      (q) GPU cost analysis — estimate compute cost for recommended D-study budgets.\n98\t    priority: P0\n99\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # pure analysis, no GPU\n100\t    hardware: none\n101\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n102\t    status: planned\n103\t\n104\t  # === P1: Important for paper strength ===\n105\t\n106\t  - id: exp-005\n107\t    claim: 2  # Scale validation\n108\t    description: >\n109\t      14B model extension: Qwen3-14B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B on datacenter GPUs\n110\t      at BF16/FP16. Tests whether variance attribution patterns change with model scale\n111\t      and architecture (dense vs reasoning-distilled).\n112\t    priority: P1\n113\t    gpu_budget_hours: 100\n114\t    hardware: TBD (needs ≥48GB VRAM per GPU)\n115\t    deps: [exp-003]\n116\t    status: planned\n117\t\n118\t  - id: exp-006\n119\t    claim: 2  # Training-time variance\n120\t    description: >\n121\t      Fine-tuning G-study: RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA.\n122\t      Fully crossed: 6 seeds × 3 learning rates × 4 data shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions\n123\t      = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 total fine-tuning runs.\n124\t      Validates whether variance hierarchy differs between inference and fine-tuning.\n125\t    priority: P1\n126\t    gpu_budget_hours: 200\n127\t    hardware: westd-32570 (RoBERTa-large fits easily on 96GB)\n128\t    deps: []\n129\t    status: planned\n130\t\n131\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n132\t\n133\t  - id: exp-007\n134\t    claim: 2  # LayerCast mitigation\n135\t    description: >\n136\t      Test LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as additional precision condition\n137\t      on MMLU. Quantifies variance reduction from this mitigation strategy.\n138\t    priority: P2\n139\t    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n140\t    hardware: westd-32570\n141\t    deps: [exp-001]\n142\t    status: planned\n143\t\n144\t  - id: exp-008\n145\t    claim: 1  # Reasoning benchmark extension — MERGED into exp-002 Phase 2\n146\t    description: >\n147\t      MATH benchmark (200 items). Merged into exp-002 D009 expansion as 5th benchmark.\n148\t      No longer a standalone experiment.\n149\t    priority: P0\n150\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # accounted in exp-002\n151\t    hardware: westd-32570\n152\t    deps: [exp-002]\n153\t    status: merged_into_exp002\n154\t\n155\t# MVP experiment (completed)\n156\tmvp:\n157\t  - id: mvp-001\n158\t    registry_id: null  # MVP was run directly, not through registry\n159\t    description: >\n160\t      MVP Phase A: 1 model (Llama-3.1-8B) × 1 hardware (RTX PRO 6000) × 3 precisions\n161\t      × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 temps × 2 orderings = 108 conditions × 50 MMLU items.\n162\t    result: >\n163\t      PASS. item_id=58.4%, precision×item=7.2%, temp×item=6.9%, prompt×item=5.7%.\n164\t      Direct precision×methodology <0.02%. G=0.357. float32 engine confound identified.\n165\t    status: completed\n166\t\n167\t# GPU budget summary (updated D009)\n168\tbudget:\n169\t  P0_total: 415  # exp-001(100✅) + exp-001b(15✅) + exp-002(300, expanded 8×5) + exp-004(0)\n170\t  P1_total: 420  # exp-003(120, descoped) + exp-005(100) + exp-006(200)\n171\t  P2_total: 30   # exp-007(30)\n172\t  grand_total: 865\n173\t  available: \"4× RTX PRO 6000 96GB (westd-32570) + 4× RTX 6000 96GB (westd-15695)\"\n174\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7213f7b-2e18-414c-bcc7-5947fa0bd98a","uuid":"1289b369-d886-4e6c-94ec-8994629d2bba","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:46:49.986Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # === P0: Must-run for paper submission ===\n\n  - id: exp-001\n    claim: 1  # Item dominance at scale\n    registry_id: exp001_llama  # also: exp001_gemma, exp001_mistral, exp001_qwen\n    description: >\n      Full-scale precision study: 4 models (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, Gemma-2-9B-IT, Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3)\n      × 3 precisions (FP32, BF16, FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings\n      × 200 MMLU items (stratified). All precisions use consistent vLLM engine (V0 enforce_eager)\n      to eliminate the float32 engine confound found in MVP. Validates item dominance finding at\n      scale and with multiple models.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 100\n    hardware: westd-32570 (RTX PRO 6000 96GB)\n    deps: []\n    status: done\n\n  - id: exp-001b\n    claim: 1  # Item dominance stability across item samples\n    registry_id: exp001b_resampling\n    description: >\n      Item resampling stability test: 3 independent stratified samples of 200 MMLU items\n      (seeds 0, 7, 99) × 1 model (Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) × 3 precisions × 3 prompts\n      × 3 seeds × 2 orderings = 54 conditions per sample. Tests whether the 58% item\n      dominance finding is stable across different item draws from MMLU, not an artifact\n      of the specific 200-item sample. Critical for defending the headline claim.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    hardware: westd-32570\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    status: done\n\n  - id: exp-002\n    claim: 1  # Item dominance generalizes + cross-benchmark gradient (also supports claim 3: benchmark-conditional budget)\n    registry_id: exp002_multi_benchmark\n    description: >\n      Multi-benchmark replication (D009 expanded): 8 models × 5 benchmarks × BF16 × 2 temps\n      × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 4 orderings × 200 items each.\n      Phase 1 (RUNNING): 4 original models × 4 benchmarks (MMLU/ARC/HellaSwag/GSM8K) on westd-32570.\n      Phase 2: + MATH as 5th benchmark (all models).\n      Phase 3: + Yi-1.5-9B, OLMo-2-7B on all 5 benchmarks (westd-15695).\n      Phase 4: + InternLM2.5-7B, DeepSeek-7B on all 5 benchmarks.\n      Validates cross-benchmark variance gradient, permutation test for monotonicity,\n      and benchmark-conditional D-study budgets.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 300\n    hardware: westd-32570 + westd-15695\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    status: running\n\n  - id: exp-003\n    claim: 2  # Separability with hardware factor\n    description: >\n      Multi-hardware G-study: 4 models × 2+ GPU types × 2 precisions (BF16, FP16)\n      × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items.\n      Tests hardware × methodology interaction. Descoped from current priority —\n      infrastructure claim narrowed to \"precision separability\" per D003/D007.\n      Would strengthen paper if second GPU type becomes available.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 120\n    hardware: TBD (needs different GPU type)\n    deps: []\n    status: descoped\n\n  - id: exp-004\n    claim: 3  # D-study reproducibility budget\n    description: >\n      Comprehensive analysis of combined exp-001/001b/002/003 data. Includes:\n      (a) Model-as-facet G-theory reanalysis — treat model as crossed random facet to properly\n      attribute model×item interaction and reduce inflated item_id/residual (Dream critical);\n      (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) on ALL variance components in ALL tables, especially\n      direct infra×method interaction term (Dream critical);\n      (c) D-study projections with CIs for optimal allocation across facets for G≥0.90/0.95/0.99,\n      with benchmark-specific budgets and comparison to IRT-based subsampling (tinyBenchmarks);\n      (d) REML vs Henderson Method I comparison as sensitivity analysis;\n      (e) Logprob-based scoring as third response variable;\n      (f) Ranking stability analysis — does precision×temperature interaction alter model rankings?\n      (g) Higher-order interaction estimation to decompose the residual component;\n      (h) G-theory vs IRT direct comparison — same MMLU data, D-study vs tinyBenchmarks IRT\n      subsampling, compare recommended item counts and discuss why G-theory is more conservative\n      (accounts for prompt/seed dimensions IRT ignores). First direct comparison in the literature;\n      (i) Power analysis — verify statistical power to detect ≥X% interaction effects given\n      5184×200 design scale, preempt \"underpowered\" reviewer concern;\n      (j) Practitioner evaluation protocol guide (Discussion/Appendix);\n      (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity — rerun G-study with temperature/ordering as fixed facets,\n      compare variance decomposition (MD2 defense);\n      (l) Binary data limitation analysis — correlate Bernoulli p(1-p) with observed item variance,\n      parallel binary vs text_exact_match analysis (MD1 defense);\n      (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife CI comparison — delete-1 jackknife as independence-safe alternative,\n      compare CI widths (MD6 defense);\n      (n) Cross-benchmark design asymmetry sensitivity — re-analyze MMLU with matched 2×2 design\n      (bf16/fp16 × T=0.0/T=0.7), compare with full 3×3 (MD8 defense);\n      (o) G-coefficient at full benchmark size — D-study projection to 14K MMLU items (MD5 defense);\n      (p) Logprob-based scoring across all benchmarks — expand from MMLU-only to all 5 benchmarks,\n      support \"Evaluation Metrics\" in title (MD9 defense);\n      (q) GPU cost analysis — estimate compute cost for recommended D-study budgets.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # pure analysis, no GPU\n    hardware: none\n    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for paper strength ===\n\n  - id: exp-005\n    claim: 2  # Scale validation\n    description: >\n      14B model extension: Qwen3-14B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B on datacenter GPUs\n      at BF16/FP16. Tests whether variance attribution patterns change with model scale\n      and architecture (dense vs reasoning-distilled).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 100\n    hardware: TBD (needs ≥48GB VRAM per GPU)\n    deps: [exp-003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: exp-006\n    claim: 2  # Training-time variance\n    description: >\n      Fine-tuning G-study: RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA.\n      Fully crossed: 6 seeds × 3 learning rates × 4 data shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions\n      = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 total fine-tuning runs.\n      Validates whether variance hierarchy differs between inference and fine-tuning.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 200\n    hardware: westd-32570 (RoBERTa-large fits easily on 96GB)\n    deps: []\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n\n  - id: exp-007\n    claim: 2  # LayerCast mitigation\n    description: >\n      Test LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as additional precision condition\n      on MMLU. Quantifies variance reduction from this mitigation strategy.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n    hardware: westd-32570\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: exp-008\n    claim: 1  # Reasoning benchmark extension — MERGED into exp-002 Phase 2\n    description: >\n      MATH benchmark (200 items). Merged into exp-002 D009 expansion as 5th benchmark.\n      No longer a standalone experiment.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # accounted in exp-002\n    hardware: westd-32570\n    deps: [exp-002]\n    status: merged_into_exp002\n\n# MVP experiment (completed)\nmvp:\n  - id: mvp-001\n    registry_id: null  # MVP was run directly, not through registry\n    description: >\n      MVP Phase A: 1 model (Llama-3.1-8B) × 1 hardware (RTX PRO 6000) × 3 precisions\n      × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 temps × 2 orderings = 108 conditions × 50 MMLU items.\n    result: >\n      PASS. item_id=58.4%, precision×item=7.2%, temp×item=6.9%, prompt×item=5.7%.\n      Direct precision×methodology <0.02%. G=0.357. float32 engine confound identified.\n    status: completed\n\n# GPU budget summary (updated D009)\nbudget:\n  P0_total: 415  # exp-001(100✅) + exp-001b(15✅) + exp-002(300, expanded 8×5) + exp-004(0)\n  P1_total: 420  # exp-003(120, descoped) + exp-005(100) + exp-006(200)\n  P2_total: 30   # exp-007(30)\n  grand_total: 865\n  available: \"4× RTX PRO 6000 96GB (westd-32570) + 4× RTX 6000 96GB (westd-15695)\"\n","numLines":174,"startLine":1,"totalLines":174}}}
